    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Buy\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan recommends Overweight, and the supplied evidence supports a constructive stance: JPM is in a confirmed uptrend across all timeframes (above rising 10 EMA, 50 SMA, 200 SMA), the golden cross is intact, RSI at 65.44 has reset from overbought with room before 70, and the 60-day +26.14% return came with a remarkably tight -0.38% drawdown. The fortress balance sheet ($3.9T assets, $317B equity) is supplied evidence. However, the missing income statement data (unverifiable ROE/NIM/credit provisions) and momentum/volume softness (negative MACD histogram, 30% below-average volume near resistance, failure to reclaim the Jan 12 high) argue against aggressive full-position buying. Therefore I initiate a Buy with roughly half the intended position at current levels (~$163.47), scaling in on either a confirmed breakout above $164.57 on expanding volume or a pullback toward the rising 50 SMA near $154.39, with a stop below the 50 SMA to protect against a trend break.\n\n**Entry Price**: 163.47\n\n**Stop Loss**: 152.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Initiate with ~half the intended overweight position (moderate sizing, do not concentrate portfolio given missing profitability data). Add on breakout above $164.57 on volume or pullback to ~$154.39.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **BUY**",
